{
  "_comment": "SHARED SETTINGS DEFINITION — the scene half of the settings pair (with scripts/shared/settings.lua, a thin derive()-only module). LAYOUT: the static `tree` is the settings window (titlebar · left page-rail paged_menu · footer · two dialogs) with EMPTY per-section containers by id (video_rows/audio_rows/kb_rows/mouse_rows/controller_rows). The hardened Rust behaviour (UnifiedSettingsScene::settings_tree) parses this tree and FILLS the containers from the row SCHEMA — the untrusted, end-user-editable Lua composes NO structure (the client is in the enemy's hands; security). settings.lua's SOLE job is turning the published section/sub-tab INDICES into the sec_*/sub_* visibility gates. STYLES: the visual skins live in `styles`; the video/audio/input row SCHEMA also still rides styles.settings.{video,audio,input} (read in place by the filler) — a data-in-styles wart to relocate to a data block in a follow-up. Realizes content-layer item #8 (settings = a real scene pair).",
